# Optional ML core runtime
# Supported ML metadata baseline.
# This file documents the secure package floor for optional editable installs.
# Checked-in installable ML locks are target-owned; only Apple Silicon is active.
#
# PLATFORM MATRIX (ADR-032):
#   OS:    Darwin (macOS)
#   ISA:   arm64 (Apple Silicon)
#   Accel: cpu (default), mps (macOS ARM64)
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Only the Apple Silicon target-owned lock is checked in as supported
# - This layer EXCLUDES platform-specific packages (rawpy, coremltools)
# - This layer EXCLUDES SAM2 due to build-time torch requirements
# - Accel is EXPLICIT via profile, never inferred from OS
#
# SECURITY NOTE:
# - Supported ML metadata now anchors on torch>=2.8.0 /
#   torchvision>=0.23.0.
# - Retired Darwin x86_64 and Linux locks are removed from installable
#   requirements surfaces and must not drive dependency graph alerts.
# - All torch.load() calls MUST use weights_only=True as defense in depth.
# - See: src/transformation_portal/core/security/torch_security.py for safe loading.
#
# See: requirements/README.md for layering rationale.

# --- PyTorch secure baseline ---
# NOTE: When updating torch versions, verify SAM2/CLIP compatibility.
